{
  "_comment": "Persistent meta-progression skill tree. A node is bought with Cores (earned across every run, per character) and applies to every map from the next run onward. Effects are either flat adds or multipliers; a node with `maxRank` above 1 can be bought repeatedly, with each rank costing `cost * costGrowth^rank`. `requires` lists node ids that must have at least one rank before this node opens.",

  "currency": "Cores",

  "_branch_note": "Four branches, each one a different answer to 'what will win me the next run'. Economy makes you richer, Warfare makes your towers stronger, Engineering makes progression cheaper, Fortification keeps the base alive. Nothing is ever chosen for you -- Cores sit in the wallet until you spend them -- so the pressure is scarcity, not exclusivity: you can eventually own everything, and the question is only which branch pays off soonest.",

